                <div class="cbc-about-section">
                    <h2>
                        About <img class="cbc-sadhana-logo"
                            src="https://cbc.gov.in/sites/default/files/2026-03/Sadhana_text.png" alt="SĀDHANA"
                            width="4313" height="1069"> Saptah
                    </h2>
                    <div class="section-about">
                        <p>
                            India's governance landscape is being reshaped by rapid technological change, renewed
                            attention to Indian Knowledge Systems, and an increasing focus on Citizen Centricity.
                            <strong><img class="cbc-sadhana-logo"
                                    src="https://cbc.gov.in/sites/default/files/2026-03/Sadhana_text.png" alt="SĀDHANA"
                                    width="4313" height="1069"> Saptah</strong> is conceived as a theme-focused,
                            sector-anchored exercise (sector classification as per SGOS) to strengthen governance
                            capability across Ministries, Departments, Organisations (MDO), and States. The structure of
                            the week shall be focused on three themes or Sutras — <strong>Technology, Tradition &amp;
                                Tangible Outcomes</strong>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            The week coincides with the Foundation Day of CBC and completion of five years of Mission
                            Karmayogi, providing an opportunity to review progress while strengthening the national
                            capacity-building ecosystem.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Through a blended delivery model—comprising Karmayogi Talks by domain experts, Samuhik
                            Charchas within institutions, digital learning through the iGOT platform, inter-ministerial
                            workshops, and training programmes conducted by civil services training institutions—the
                            initiative will engage civil servants across the government ecosystem. Participation will
                            extend across <strong>93 Central Ministries and Departments, 30 States and UTs</strong>
                            implementing Mission Karmayogi, and more than <strong>200 civil services training
                                institutions</strong>, supported through coordinated institutional mechanisms led by
                            CBC.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Beyond a week of learning engagements, <img class="cbc-sadhana-logo"
                                src="https://cbc.gov.in/sites/default/files/2026-03/Sadhana_text.png" alt="SĀDHANA"
                                width="4313" height="1069"> Saptah aims to reinforce a culture of continuous learning in
                            government, accelerate engagement with the digital learning ecosystem, strengthen knowledge
                            exchange across institutions, and generate insights for strengthening the broader
                            capacity-building architecture under Mission Karmayogi.
                        </p>
